      "side": 1,
      "message": "Thanks for the review, George! \nThat rename (5236ec54) is the one the first paragraph of the commit message cites — the include was added three months after the rename, so it has never matched anything.\n\nI did test the re-point first (re-verified today on a fresh boot):\non a bletchley QEMU image the test fails in its Test Setup before the body runs. \"Redfish Power Off\" enters the boot-test framework, whose Auto_reboot/cp_setup plug-in PATCHes /redfish/v1/Systems/system (\"Boot\"/\"AutomaticRetryConfig\") and gets HTTP 500, so OBMC Boot Test aborts with \"Plug-in setup failed.\" — the same failure the two SoftwareInventory includes already in QEMU_CI show on my setup.\n\nbletchley is the only target I can test, though. If the QEMU target CI runs this list against can execute this suite\u0027s setup, re-pointing is strictly better than dropping (it restores UpdateService coverage) and I\u0027ll gladly update the change to do that. Which QEMU target does CI use for this list?",
